<title>SINGAPORE: IPC expects difficult market to continue.</title>
<headline>IPC expects difficult market to continue.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-08-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Personal computer maker IPC Corp said on Tuesday it expects difficult market conditions to continue for the rest of 1996.</p>
<p>The company just announced that its first half net profit fell 85 percent to Singapore $5.32 million.</p>
<p>For six months ended June 30, turnover fell to S$738.4 million against S$833.8 million previously.</p>
<p>In a note accompanying its results, IPC said turnover fell after it closed its retail operations in the U.S. and because of difficult market conditions in Europe.</p>
<p>- Singapore Newsroom 65-8703080</p>
